{
  "title": "Ziyarah of Imam Husayn (a) at the Qadr Nights",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Shaykh Muhammad ibn al-Mashhadi has reported, through considerable chains of authority, that Imam al-Sadiq (a) said the following: if you want to visit Imam al-Husayn (a) at the Qadr Nights, you may come to his holy shrine after you wash yourself and put on the cleanest of your clothes. When you stop at his tomb, face it, making the qiblah direction between your shoulders, and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nASSALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA RASOOLIL LAAH\nPeace be upon you, O son of Allah's Messenger,\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nASSALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA AMEERIL MU'MINEEN\npeace be upon you, O son of the Commander of the Faithful,\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ الصِّدِّيْقَةِ الطَّاهِرَةِ فَاطِمَةَ سَيِّدَةِ نِسَاۤءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nASSALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNAS SIDDEEQATIT TAAHIRATI FAATIMATA SAYYIDATI NISAAA-IL A'AALAMEEN\npeace be upon you, O son of the veracious, immaculate lady Fatimah, chief of the women of the worlds,\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَوْلَايَ يَاۤ اَبَا عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nASSALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAWLAAYA YAA ABAA A'BDILLAAHI WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\npeace be upon you, O my master, Abu Abdillah, and Allah's mercy and blessings be upon you.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ اَقَمْتَ الصَّلَاةَ وَاٰتَيْتَ الزَّكَاةَ وَاَمَرْتَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَنَهَيْتَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَتَلَوْتَ الْكِتَابَ حَقَّ تِلَاوَتِهٖ وَجَاهَدْتَ فِي اللّٰهِ حَقَّ جِهَادِهٖ وَصَبَرْتَ عَلَى الْاَذٰى فِيْ جَنْبِهٖ مُحْتَسِبًا حَتّٰى اَتَاكَ الْيَقِيْنُ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA QAD AQAMTAS SALAATA WA AATAYTAZ ZAKAATA WA AMARTA BIL MA'ROOFI WA NAHAYTA A'NIL MUNKARI WA TALAWTAL KITAABA HAQQA TILAAWATIHI WA JAAHADTA FILLAAHI HAQQA JIHAADIHI WA SABARTA A'LAL AZAA FEE JAMBIHI MUHTASIBAN HATTAA ATAAKAL YAQEEN\nI bear witness that you performed the prayers, defrayed the poor-rate, enjoined the right, forbade the wrong, recited the Book as exactly as it should be recited, strove for the sake of Allah as exactly as striving must be, and faced all troubles steadfastly for His sake, seeking His reward, until death came upon you.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ خَالَفُوْكَ وَحَارَبُوْكَ وَالَّذِيْنَ خَذَلُوْكَ وَالَّذِيْنَ قَتَلُوْكَ مَلْعُوْنُوْنَ عَلٰى لِسَانِ النَّبِيِّ الْاُمِّيِّ وَقَدْ خَابَ مَنِ افْتَرٰى\nASH-HADU ANNAL LAZEENA KHAALAFOOKA WA HAARABOOKA WAL LAZEENA KHAZALOOKA WAL LAZEENA QATALOOKA MAL-U'NOONA A'LAA LISAANIN NABIYYIL UMMIYYI WA QAD KHAABA MANIF TARAA\nI also bear witness that those who dissented from you, those who fought against you, those who let you down, and those who slew you — all of them were accursed by the tongue of the unlettered Prophet, and he who forges lies indeed fails to attain his desire.\nلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ الظَّالِمِيْنَ لَكُمْ مِنَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَ وَضَاعَفَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْعَذَابَ الْاَلِيْمَ\nLA-A'NALLAAHUZ ZAALIMEENA LAKUM MINAL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREEN WA DAAA-A'FA A'LAYHIMUL A'ZAABAL ALEEM\nMay Allah curse those who wronged you, from among the past and the present generations, and may He double for them the painful torment.\nاَتَيْتُكَ يَا مَوْلَايَ يَا ابْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ زَاۤئِرًا عَارِفًا بِحَقِّكَ مُوَالِيًا لِاَوْلِيَاۤئِكَ مُعَادِيًا لِاَعْدَاۤئِكَ مُسْتَبْصِرًا بِالْهُدَى الَّذِيۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْهِ عَارِفًا بِضَلَالَةِ مَنْ خَالَفَكَ فَاشْفَعْ لِيْ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ\nATAYTUKA YAA MAWLAAYA YABNA RASOOLILLAAHI ZAAA-IRAN A'AARIFAM BI-HAQQIKA MUWAALIYAL LI-AWLIYAAA-IKA MU'AADIYAL LI-A'DAAA-IKA MUSTABSIRAM BIL HUDAL LAZEE ANTA A'LAYHI A'AARIFAM BI-DALAALATI MAN KHAALAFAK, FASH-FA' LEE I'NDA RABBIK\nO my master and son of Allah's Messenger, I have come to you visiting you, acknowledging the standing that you enjoy, declaring my loyalty to those who are loyal to you, renouncing your enemies, seeking to follow the true guidance that you are following, and recognizing the deviation of those who oppose you; so, please intercede for me before your Lord.\nYou may then throw yourself on the tomb, kiss it, put your cheek on it, move yourself towards the place of the head, and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ فِيۤ اَرْضِهٖ وَسَمَاۤئِهٖ\nASSALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HUJJATALLAAHI FEE ARDIHI WA SAMAAA-IH\nPeace be upon you, O Argument of Allah in His lands and heavens.\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى رُوْحِكَ الطَّيِّبِ وَجَسَدِكَ الطَّاهِرِ وَعَلَيْكَ السَّلَامُ يَا مَوْلَايَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAA ROOHIKAT TAYYIBI WA JASADIKAT TAAHIR, WA A'LAYKAS SALAAMU YAA MAWLAAYA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nMay Allah bless your immaculate spirit and your pure body. Peace, and Allah's mercy and blessings, be upon you, O my master.\nYou may again throw yourself on the tomb, kiss it, put your cheek on it, move yourself towards the place of the head, and offer the two-unit prayer of ziyarah, after which you may offer any possible amount of prayer units. You may then turn to the side of the feet and visit 'Ali ibn al-Husayn, saying:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَوْلَايَ وَابْنَ مَوْلَايَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ لَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ ظَلَمَكَ وَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ قَتَلَكَ وَضَاعَفَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْعَذَابَ الْاَلِيْمَ\nASSALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAWLAAYA WABNA MAWLAAYA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH, LA-A'NALLAAHU MAN ZALAMAK WA LA-A'NALLAAHU MAN QATALAK WA DAAA-A'FA A'LAYHIMUL A'ZAABAL ALEEM\nPeace be upon you, O my master and son of my master, and Allah's mercy and blessings. May Allah curse those who wronged you. May Allah curse those who slew you. May Allah double the painful chastisement for them.\nYou may then pray to Allah for your personal needs. Then leave your place at the side of the feet towards the qiblah direction in order to visit the martyrs, saying:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ اَيُّهَا الصِّدِّيْقُوْنَ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ اَيُّهَا الشُّهَدَاۤءُ الصَّابِرُوْنَ\nASSALAAMU A'LAYKUM AYYUHAS SIDDEEQOON, ASSALAAMU A'LAYKUM AYYUHASH SHUHADAAA-ISS SAABIROON\nPeace be upon you, O veracious ones. Peace be upon you, O steadfast martyrs.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكُمْ جَاهَدْتُمْ فِيْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَصَبَرْتُمْ عَلَى الْاَذٰى فِيْ جَنْبِ اللّٰهِ وَنَصَحْتُمْ لِلّٰهِ وَلِرَسُوْلِهٖ حَتّٰى اَتَاكُمُ الْيَقِيْنُ\nASH-HADU ANNAKUM JAAHADTUM FEE SABEELILLAAHI WA SABARTUM A'LAL AZAA FEE JAMBILLAAHI WA NASAHTUM LILLAAHI WA LI-RASOOLIHI HATTAA ATAAKUMUL YAQEEN\nI bear witness that you strove in the way of Allah, acted patiently against harm for the sake of Allah, and did sincerely for the sake of Allah and His Messenger until death came upon you.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكُمْ اَحْيَاۤءٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ تُرْزَقُوْنَ\nASH-HADU ANNAKUM AHYAAA-UN I'NDA RABBIKUM TURZAQOON\nI bear witness that you are alive and are being provided sustenance from your Lord.\nفَجَزَاكُمُ اللّٰهُ عَنِ الْاِسْلَامِ وَاَهْلِهٖ اَفْضَلَ جَزَاۤءِ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ وَجَمَعَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ فِيْ مَحَلِّ النَّعِيْمِ\nFA-JAZAAKUMULLAAHU A'NIL ISLAAMI WA AHLIHI AFDALA JAZAAA-IL MUHSINEEN WA JAMA'A BAYNANAA WA BAYNAKUM FEE MAHALLIN NA'EEM\nMay Allah reward you with the best reward of the good-doers on behalf of Islam and its people, and may He join us to you in the abode of bliss.\nYou may then walk to the shrine of al-'Abbas, son of the Commander of the Faithful. When you stop at the gate of the shrine, say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ اَمِيرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْعَبْدُ الصَّالِحُ الْمُطِيْعُ لِلّٰهِ وَلِرَسُوْلِهٖ\nASSALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA AMEERIL MU'MINEEN, ASSALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL A'BDUS SAALIHUL MUTEE-U'L LILLAAHI WA LI-RASOOLIH\nPeace be upon you, O son of the Commander of the Faithful. Peace be upon you, O righteous servant of Allah, obedient to Allah and to His Messenger.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ جَاهَدْتَ وَنَصَحْتَ وَصَبَرْتَ حَتّٰى اَتَاكَ الْيَقِيْنُ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA QAD JAAHADTA WA NASAHTA WA SABARTA HATTAA ATAAKAL YAQEEN\nI bear witness that you strove, acted sincerely, and tolerated harm until death came upon you.\nلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ الظَّالِمِيْنَ لَكُمْ مِنَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَ وَاَلْحَقَهُمْ بِدَرَكِ الْجَحِيْمِ\nLA-A'NALLAAHUZ ZAALIMEENA LAKUM MINAL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREENA WA ALHAQAHUM BI-DARAKIL JAHEEM\nMay Allah curse those who wronged you, from the past and the present generations, and may He send them to the lowest layer of the blazing Hell.\nYou may offer there any amount of prayers voluntarily, and then leave.",
  "merits": "Numerous traditions state the merits of visiting Imam al-Husayn (a) during the month of Ramadan in general, and at the first, fifteenth, and last night of this month in particular, and at the Qadr Nights more specifically.\nImam Muhammad al-Taqi (al-Jawad) is reported to have said, \"If one visits al-Husayn (a) at the twenty-third night of Ramadan, which is hoped to be the Qadr Night at which every affair of wisdom is made clear, he will be shaken hands by the spirits of twenty-four thousand prophets, all of whom ask Almighty Allah to permit them to visit al-Husayn (a) at that night.\"\nAccording to another validly reported tradition, Imam al-Sadiq (a) has said, \"At the Qadr Night, a caller from the seventh sky will call out from inside the Divine Throne: verily, Almighty Allah has forgiven anyone who comes to the tomb of al-Husayn.\"\nAccording to another report, everyone who presents himself at the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a) at the Qadr Night, offers a two-unit prayer therein (or any number of prayers possible), beseeches Almighty Allah to grant him Paradise, and seeks Him to protect him against Hellfire, then Almighty Allah shall grant him what he has asked for and shall save him from what he has asked Him to protect from.\nIbn Qawlawayh has reported Imam al-Sadiq (a) as saying, \"One who is on his way to visit the tomb of al-Husayn ibn 'Ali (a) in the month of Ramadan but dies on the way, he shall be neither stopped for interrogation nor called to account. Moreover, he shall be allowed to enter Paradise without being exposed to horror.\"\nThe words by which Imam al-Husayn (a) is visited at the Qadr Night are a form of ziyarah mentioned by Shaykh al-Mufid, Muhammad ibn al-Mashhadi, Ibn Tawus, and al-Shahid — Allah's mercy be upon them all — in their books on forms of ziyarah. They dedicated these forms to the ziyarah at this night and on the two days of 'Id (i.e. 'Id al-Fitr and 'Id al-Azha).",
